# Paper draft figure paths

Cursor’s markdown preview often resolves image paths from the **workspace root**, not from `paper/`. Relative `figures/...` links then 404 and the draft looks broken (missing images everywhere).

## Required link form

In `paper/draft.md`, every figure must use a **workspace-root absolute** path:

```markdown
![Figure N. caption without underscores](/paper/figures/demo/fig01_trie.svg)
```

**Image alt/caption text must not contain `_` or `\( ... \)` LaTeX.** Markdown treats `_xh_` as emphasis and can break the `![...](url)` parse so the figure never renders. Write `Wxh` / `Whh` in alts; keep LaTeX in body prose only.

## Do not

- `](figures/...)` — breaks Cursor preview (looks for repo-root `figures/`)
- `](paper/figures/...)` — breaks VS Code file-relative preview (`paper/paper/figures/`)
- `](./figures/...)` — same class of breakage
- Convert to HTML `<img>` tags as a workaround
- Flip path styles back and forth while “debugging” preview

## Preview settings (already in repo)

`.vscode/settings.json` should keep:

- `"workbench.editorAssociations": { "*.md": "vscode.markdown.preview.editor" }`
- `"markdown.styles": ["paper/markdown-preview.css"]` (light paper CSS over Abyss)

When editing the draft, if images vanish again, check paths match `/paper/figures/...` first — do not invent new preview scripts.
